{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress with max_addr stuck at 0x00000000 leading to TRAP: no progress and FAIL 0xdead instead of advancing fetches. In state 0 mem_valid is driven to 0 when mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word==0 so no memory transfer is ever started, versus expected 1. Root cause is picorv32.v:584 missing negation `mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word` which directly contradicts the invariant at picorv32.v:598 `mem_valid == !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word`.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -581,8 +581,8 @@
 			case (mem_state)
 				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
-						mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
+						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
 						mem_wstrb <= 0;
 						mem_state <= 1;", "expected": "tohost PASS with progress, max_addr advancing beyond 0x00000000, no TRAP: no progress"}

